  "turn": 1,
  "user": "Please look up transaction TX-0401 in my account records and verify its amount. Then explain which reason codes could apply; I have not yet told you what happened.",
  "answer": "I found TX-0401 and verified its amount.\n\n**TX-0401**\n- Date: 2026-07-20\n- Merchant: TechMart Online\n- Amount: **EUR 240.00** (debit, card payment)\n- Status: settled\n- Account: ACC-1005 (EUR)\n\nYour records also show **TX-0402**, dated 2026-07-14, for the same amount (EUR 240.00) at the same merchant, TechMart Online. I mention it only because it matches TX-0401 exactly. I have not drawn any conclusion from it.\n\nThese are the dispute reason codes I can open, and what each one covers:\n\n- **duplicate_charge**: the same purchase was charged more than once. This could fit if TX-0401 and TX-0402 are two charges for one purchase.\n- **fraud_card_not_present**: you did not make the online card payment and someone used your card details without authorization.\n- **unauthorized_debit**: the debit was taken from your account without your permission.\n- **goods_not_received**: you paid, but the goods were never delivered.\n- **service_not_rendered**: you paid, but the service was never provided.\n\nWhich of these fits depends on what happened. If you tell me, I will check eligibility before anything is filed. No dispute has been opened.",
